<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	The Intune MAM SDK stores policy, tokens and its device identity in the keychain, and
	shares some of it with the broker in a separate process. Without these groups every
	keychain write fails with -34018 (errSecMissingEntitlement) and nothing works — the
	SDK logs "Could not store per-install keychain items" and enrollment ends in
	authorizationNeeded.

	Order matters (CLAUDE.md): the app's own bundle ID first, then the SDK's group, then
	MSAL's cache group. On a real consumer app IntuneMAMConfigurator writes these; here
	they are checked in so the example builds without that step.
	-->
	<key>keychain-access-groups</key>
	<array>
		<string>$(AppIdentifierPrefix)intune.example</string>
		<string>$(AppIdentifierPrefix)com.microsoft.intune.mam</string>
		<string>$(AppIdentifierPrefix)com.microsoft.adalcache</string>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
